    raw_med = [("In agriculture domain expertise, what is 'Precision Agriculture'?", 'An agricultural management strategy using GPS, IoT sensors, satellite imagery, and AI to optimize field-level inputs (water, fertilizer, seeds)', ['Plowing farm fields using manual hand bullock carts', 'Planting the identical crop across an entire national state', 'Spraying uniform high chemical doses over all farm acreage'], 'Precision farming reduces input costs and chemical runoff by tailoring irrigation and nutrients to micro-variations across soil zones.'), ("In agricultural soil science, what does 'Soil Cation Exchange Capacity' (CEC) measure?", 'The total capacity of a soil to hold, retain, and exchange positively charged nutrient ions (e.g., Ca2+, Mg2+, K+, NH4+)', ['The rate at which water evaporates from surface soil', 'The total mass of earthworms living inside one acre of soil', 'The mechanical hardness of dry agricultural clay'], 'High CEC soils (e.g., humus and clay soils) hold abundant nutrients against leaching, releasing them steadily to plant roots.'), ("In public health domain analytics, what is the 'Basic Reproduction Number' (R0) of an infectious disease?", 'The expected average number of secondary infections generated by a single infected individual in a completely susceptible population', ['The percentage of infected patients who die from the disease', 'The number of days required to manufacture a vaccine in laboratories', 'The total financial expenditure incurred on quarantine hospital beds'], 'If R0 > 1, the disease spreads exponentially into an epidemic; if R0 < 1, the transmission chain gradually dies out.'), ("In epidemiology, what is 'Case Fatality Rate' (CFR) versus 'Infection Fatality Rate' (IFR)?", 'CFR is deaths divided by confirmed diagnosed cases; IFR is deaths divided by total estimated infections (including asymptomatic cases)', ['CFR is for hospital patients; IFR is for animals', 'CFR is calculated before an outbreak; IFR after an outbreak', 'There is zero difference; both terms are identical'], 'IFR reflects true biological lethality across all infected individuals, and is typically lower than CFR because many mild cases go unrecorded.'), ("In urban planning, what is 'Floor Space Index' (FSI) or 'Floor Area Ratio' (FAR)?", 'The ratio of the total covered built-up floor area of a building to the total area of the plot on which it stands', ['The physical height of a building measured in feet', 'The percentage of plot area covered by green grass lawns', 'The number of parking slots provided in the basement'], 'FSI governs urban density: if a 1,000 sq m plot has an FSI of 2.0, total allowable built-up construction across all floors is 2,000 sq m.'), ("In environmental engineering, what does 'BOD' (Biochemical Oxygen Demand) measure in water quality testing?", 'The amount of dissolved oxygen required by aerobic microorganisms to biologically decompose organic matter in a water sample', ['The total weight of plastic garbage floating on river surfaces', 'The chemical acidity measured on a standard pH sensor', 'The temperature difference between river surface and bottom'], 'High BOD indicates severe organic sewage pollution, depleting dissolved oxygen and killing aquatic fish populations.'), ("In water testing, what is 'COD' (Chemical Oxygen Demand) and how does it compare to BOD?", 'COD measures total oxygen required to chemically oxidize both biodegradable and non-biodegradable organic pollutants; COD is always higher than BOD', ['COD measures only drinking water mineral salts', 'COD is always lower than BOD because chemicals are weak', 'COD measures bacterial pathogens using microscopes'], 'COD provides a rapid measure (completed in hours, whereas standard BOD takes 5 days) of total chemical industrial organic pollution.'), ("In the electrical power grid, what does 'Grid Frequency' stability reflect in India (standard 50.00 Hz)?", 'The real-time dynamic balance between total active electrical generation and total consumer power demand across the synchronous grid', ['The speed at which coal trains travel to thermal power plants', 'The percentage of electricity generated from nuclear power stations', 'The voltage reading of household electrical wall sockets'], 'If demand exceeds generation, frequency drops below 50 Hz; if generation exceeds demand, frequency rises, risking catastrophic blackouts.'), ("In power transmission, what is 'Ancillary Services' in grid operations?", 'Operational support services (frequency regulation, spinning reserves, reactive power voltage support) contracted by the grid operator to maintain stability', ['Cleaning dust off solar photovoltaic glass panels', 'Writing monthly electricity bills for residential customers', 'Trimming tree branches growing near wooden power poles'], 'Ancillary services ensure the grid remains resilient and stable amid intermittency from renewable wind and solar generation.'), ("In renewable energy integration, what is the 'Duck Curve' phenomenon in solar-rich power grids?", 'A daily net load curve showing a deep mid-day belly (due to abundant solar power) followed by a steep evening ramp when the sun sets', ['A curve plotting the migratory flight paths of wild ducks over wind turbines', 'A chart tracking the retail market price of roasted poultry meat', 'A graph showing seasonal river water discharges through hydro dams'], 'The duck curve poses acute challenges: grid operators must rapidly ramp up flexible conventional or battery capacity as solar drops at twilight.'), ("In banking domain analytics, what is the 'Net Non-Performing Asset' (NNPA) ratio?", 'NNPA = (Gross NPAs - Provisions) / (Gross Advances - Provisions)', ['NNPA = Total Bank Deposits / Total Loans Given', 'NNPA = Total Cash in Vaults / Total Balance Sheet Assets', 'NNPA = Total Executive Salaries / Annual Net Profit'], "NNPA reflects the true bad debt risk exposure remaining on a bank's balance sheet after subtracting financial loss provisions."), ("In banking domain regulation, what is the 'Liquidity Coverage Ratio' (LCR) under Basel III?", 'The requirement that banks hold sufficient High-Quality Liquid Assets (HQLA) to survive a severe 30-day liquidity stress scenario', ['The ratio of long-term mortgages to equity share capital', 'The percentage of bank branches equipped with automated cash ATMs', 'The annual dividend percentage paid out to corporate shareholders'], 'LCR guarantees that a bank holds unencumbered cash and sovereign bonds to absorb sudden wholesale depositor runs for a month.'), ("In the insurance domain, what does 'Incurred Claims Ratio' (ICR) evaluate for an insurance company?", 'The total value of claims paid and provisions created divided by the total net earned premium collected (Claims / Premium * 100)', ['The percentage of insurance policy applications rejected due to illness', 'The average annual bonus paid to licensed insurance sales agents', 'The market valuation of the insurance company on the stock exchange'], 'An ICR of ~70-80% indicates sound underwriting profitability; an ICR over 100% means claims exceed premium revenues, causing underwriting losses.'), ("In education domain assessment under NEP 2020, what is 'PARAKH'?", 'Performance Assessment, Review, and Analysis of Knowledge for Holistic Development (national assessment center setting standard evaluation norms)', ['A digital tablet given to high school physics students', 'A national athletic sports championship held for universities', 'A scholarship scheme funding overseas foreign education'], 'PARAKH operates under NCERT, setting standardized psychometric norms, national achievement surveys (NAS), and holistic report cards.'), ("In education pedagogy, what is the 'Competency-Based Education' (CBE) paradigm shift?", 'Moving from rote memorization and rigid syllabus completion to demonstrating mastery of observable, real-world competencies and learning outcomes', ['Grading students exclusively on the number of pages they write in exams', 'Forcing all students to study only mechanical vocational trades', 'Conducting oral examination debates without any written textbooks'], 'CBE emphasizes deep comprehension, critical application, problem-solving, and individualized learning pace over passive seat-time.'), ("In environmental regulation, what is the 'Air Quality Index' (AQI) and how is it determined?", 'A composite index converting concentrations of 8 key ambient air pollutants (PM10, PM2.5, NO2, SO2, CO, O3, NH3, Pb) into a single numeric score', ['A measure of ambient outdoor air temperature and humidity', 'The percentage of oxygen present in local city atmosphere', 'The wind direction recorded by airport weather radars'], 'AQI simplifies complex chemical telemetry into color-coded categories (Good, Moderate, Poor, Severe) to communicate health hazards.'), ("In environmental domain law, what does 'CRZ' (Coastal Regulation Zone) notification regulate?", 'Development activities, construction, and industries within 500 meters of the High Tide Line (HTL) along coastal shorelines and tidally influenced water bodies', ['Deep-sea commercial international petroleum tanker routes', 'The extraction of freshwater from inland mountain glaciers', 'The commercial breeding of livestock cattle on rural plains'], 'CRZ notifications protect fragile coastal ecosystems (mangroves, coral reefs) while balancing livelihoods of traditional fishing communities.'), ("In defense domain strategy, what is 'Network-Centric Warfare' (NCW)?", 'Translating an information advantage into competitive warfighting power by robustly networking sensors, command decision-makers, and shooters', ['Engaging in cyber warfare to hack commercial retail bank websites', 'Using public social media websites to recruit military infantry soldiers', 'Laying physical copper telephone wires between military barracks'], 'NCW improves situational awareness, accelerates decision cycles (OODA loop), and enables rapid, synchronized precision kinetic strikes.'), ("In defense domain logistics, what does 'Indigenization' target under positive indigenization lists?", 'Banning the import of designated defense weapon systems, platforms, and sub-systems to compel indigenous design and manufacturing in India', ['Exporting all domestic military hardware to foreign armed forces', 'Recruiting only native soldiers born in border districts', 'Scrapping all existing armored tanks and artillery guns'], "MoD's positive indigenization lists stimulate private defense manufacturing clusters and enhance sovereign technological autonomy."), ("In healthcare domain quality, what is 'NABH' accreditation in India?", 'National Accreditation Board for Hospitals & Healthcare Providers (standard for patient safety, clinical quality, and hospital governance)', ['National Association of Blood Donors and Hospital Workers', 'Network of Ayurvedic Biomedicine and Herbal Clinics', 'National Agency for Biological Hazards and Viral Disease'], 'NABH standards benchmark clinical protocols, infection control, medication safety, and patient rights across Indian hospitals.'), ("In telecom engineering, what is 'Spectrum Refarming'?", 'Reallocating legacy frequency bands (e.g., 900 MHz or 1800 MHz formerly used for 2G/3G) to modern high-efficiency 4G/5G mobile broadband', ['Selling damaged telecommunication cellular tower metal scrap', 'Digging up underground optical fiber broadband cables for cleaning', 'Using radio broadcasting antennas to dry agricultural grains'], 'Spectrum refarming extracts maximum spectral efficiency from prime sub-GHz coverage spectrum without requiring new frequency allocations.'), ("In transportation infrastructure, what is 'Ballastless Track' (Slab Track) in modern high-speed rail systems?", 'Railway tracks laid on reinforced concrete slabs rather than traditional crushed stone ballast gravel beds', ['Rail lines constructed without any steel metal rails', 'Tracks built on floating inflatable pontoons over water rivers', 'Underground railway tunnels built without concrete tunnel walls'], 'Slab tracks provide superior geometric stability at high speeds (>250 km/h), eliminate flying ballast hazards, and drastically reduce maintenance.'), ("In civil structural engineering, what does 'Pre-stressed Concrete' (PSC) achieve over standard reinforced concrete?", 'Engineers apply compressive stresses using high-strength steel tendons before loading, counteracting tensile stresses under service loads', ['Concrete poured without adding any water or moisture during mixing', 'Using painted plastic fibers instead of steel reinforcement bars', 'Pre-heating wet concrete blocks inside industrial ovens'], 'PSC enables longer bridge spans, thinner structural decks, and crack-free longevity under heavy dynamic vehicular loads.'), ("In mining and geology domain management, what is 'Overburden' (OB)?", 'The layer of soil, rock, and vegetation that lies above an underground mineral or coal seam that must be removed in open-cast mining', ['The excessive weight of mineral ore loaded onto a transport truck', 'The financial debt owed by a commercial mining corporation to banks', 'The psychological stress experienced by deep underground miners'], 'The Stripping Ratio (volume of OB removed per ton of coal mined) dictates the economic viability of surface opencast mining.'), ("In climate change domain science, what does 'Global Warming Potential' (GWP) measure?", 'How much energy the emissions of 1 ton of a specific greenhouse gas will absorb over a given period (e.g., 100 years), relative to 1 ton of CO2', ['The maximum summer temperature recorded on global deserts', 'The melting speed of polar ice caps measured in meters per year', 'The total electricity generated by global solar photovoltaic panels'], 'GWP allows comparison of different gases: Methane (CH4) has a GWP of ~28 over 100 years; Sulfur Hexafluoride (SF6) exceeds 23,000.'), ("In international carbon markets, what is 'Article 6' of the Paris Agreement governing?", 'Market and non-market mechanisms for international cooperation, carbon emissions trading, and Internationally Transferred Mitigation Outcomes (ITMOs)', ['The immediate dissolution of all international coal mining industries', 'The deployment of military forces to enforce forest protections', 'The calculation of sovereign debt write-offs for poor nations'], 'Article 6.2 and 6.4 establish rigorous accounting rules to prevent double-counting of carbon credits transferred between nations.'), ("In forest management domain governance, what is 'CAMPA' in India?", 'Compensatory Afforestation Fund Management and Planning Authority (managing funds collected for diversion of forest land to non-forest purposes)', ['Central Agency for Mountain Protection and Agriculture', 'Committee for Animal Management and Preservation in Asia', 'Commercial Agro-forestry Marketing Promotion Authority'], 'CAMPA funds collected under the Forest Conservation Act are deployed to afforest non-forest land and regenerate degraded forest tracts.'), ("In food grain supply chain logistics, what is 'Silo' storage versus traditional 'Cover and Plinth' (CAP) storage?", 'Silos are mechanized, temperature-controlled, hermetic vertical metal cylinders; CAP stores bagged grains on plinths covered by plastic tarpaulins', ['Silos are underground caves dug into mountain hills', 'CAP uses automated air-conditioned concrete warehouses', 'Silos store liquid chemicals; CAP stores solid coal'], 'Modern steel silos eliminate rodent infestations, prevent fungal moisture spoilage, and automate bulk grain loading into railway wagons.'), ("In public health sanitation, what does 'Faecal Sludge Management' (FSM) entail in non-sewered urban areas?", 'The safe emptying, transport, treatment, and resource recovery (co-composting, biochar) of human excreta from on-site septic tanks and pit latrines', ['Dumping raw septic waste directly into municipal storm drains', 'Using untreated human waste as drinking water for farm livestock', 'Paving asphalt over full septic tanks without ever emptying them'], 'FSM is critical for achieving ODF Plus Plus status, preventing raw pathogen discharge into urban groundwater and water bodies.'), ("In electrical domain engineering, what is 'Power Factor' and why do industrial utilities penalize low power factor?", 'The ratio of Real Power (kW) to Apparent Power (kVA); a low power factor draws excessive reactive current, causing line losses and grid strain', ['The ratio of solar energy to thermal coal generation', 'The price charged per kilowatt-hour of electric power', 'The mechanical horsepower generated by electric vehicle motors'], 'Utilities mandate power factors near unity (0.95 to 1.0), requiring industries to install capacitor banks to correct lagging inductive loads.'), ("In railway signaling domain engineering, what does 'ETCS' stand for in train collision protection?", 'European Train Control System (an automatic train protection standard ensuring trains do not exceed authorized speeds or pass red signals)', ['Electronic Ticket Collection Service', 'Emergency Track Crossing Standard', 'Engine Temperature Control Sensor'], 'ETCS uses trackside balises and GSM-R/LTE wireless communication to continuously supervise train movements and apply emergency brakes automatically.'), ("What is 'KAVACH' in Indian Railways signaling and safety domain technology?", 'An indigenous Automatic Train Protection (ATP) system designed to prevent train collisions (SPAD, head-on, rear-end) and enforce speed limits', ['A bulletproof metal armor installed around locomotive engines', 'An electronic mobile ticketing application for passenger booking', 'A track cleaning machine that removes trash from railway lines'], 'KAVACH continuously transmits safety movement authorities via UHF radio, automatically applying locomotive brakes if the driver fails to act.'), ("In electric vehicle (EV) charging domain infrastructure, what does 'CCS' stand for in DC fast charging?", 'Combined Charging System (a standard connector combining AC charging pins with two high-power DC pins)', ['Centralized Current Switchboard', 'Controlled Continuous Supercharger', 'Core Charging Substation'], 'CCS (Combo 1 and Combo 2) allows an EV to use a single inlet for both slow AC home charging and high-power DC highway fast charging.')]
